// TEST: Tuple With One Component Type (rejects)
// ERROR: BL1004
// ERROR-CONTAINS: needs at least TWO component types
// `Tuple<T>` is the component-typed spelling's version of `Tuple<1>` (`005`),
// and it is refused for the same reason: there is no 1-tuple in Blade, `(e)`
// is grouping (formalism.md 1275). The two spellings must agree about this or
// one of them becomes a back door to a degenerate one-element IRTTuple.
function g(p: Tuple<Float64>) -> Float64 = p[0]
// EXPECT: parse failure -- a component-typed Tuple needs at least two components
